  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the dehumanizing visual metaphor",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of the mating baboons, which serves as the central metaphor for the meme. The user is implicitly identifying with or projecting their own judgment, disgust, or moral stance onto the visual of the baboons, which is then mapped onto the human scandal referenced in the text. This projection is not explicit (e.g., no 'you' or 'me' text), but it is implied through the user's engagement with the meme's hateful intent — the user is projecting their own dehumanizing perspective onto the visual material, which is then used to demean the subjects. The projection is onto the VisualMaterial entity 'two_baboons' as the primary metaphorical anchor.",
